  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S5 restores a mandatory per-model recall at 8 incidents per 100,000 with no alternative, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k). S2 keeps a 5% cap but has no stop-sale: models above the limit may keep selling indefinitely under regulator-approved safeguards, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). Both companies' confidentiality and suppression/shut-off positions are largely met within acceptable ranges."
